cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "moseslukeprismagraphpy: PRISMA 2020 flow diagrams in Python"
version: 0.1.1
date-released: 2026-11-06
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24004986
authors:
  - family-names: Luke
    given-names: Moses
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0600-6660"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Moses-L/prismaflow"
abstract: >-
  Python package and command-line tool for creating PRISMA 2020 systematic review flow
  diagrams from screening counts or a CSV template. Calculates downstream counts, validates
  them, and exports PNG, SVG, PDF and interactive HTML. An independent reimplementation
  inspired by the PRISMA2020 R package; not affiliated with the PRISMA group.
keywords:
  - PRISMA 2020
  - systematic review
  - meta-analysis
  - flow diagram
  - evidence synthesis
